// Seven 1024-byte echoes form one flight without TCP timestamps.
// The peer retains segments 1, 3, 5 and 6, leaving holes at 0, 2 and 4.
// Three duplicate ACKs repair the first hole. Each following partial ACK
// repairs the next hole immediately, before the 300 ms RTO.
// Receive window 23040 units: the peer's MSS 1024 caps each of the 90 admitted frames
// (128 KiB / 1460) at 1024 bytes, 92160 bytes >> shift 2. The SYN-ACK stays 65535
// (unscaled cap); 92160 < 2 x 65535, so no window-update ACK follows the handshake.

0     < S 0:0(0) win 64240 <mss 1024,nop,nop,sackOK,nop,wscale 7>
+0    > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,wscale 2,sackOK,eol,eol,eol>
+0    < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 502
+0    < P. 1:1025(1024) ack 1 win 502
+0    > P. 1:1025(1024) ack 1025 win 23040
+0    < P. 1025:2049(1024) ack 1 win 502
+0    > P. 1025:2049(1024) ack 2049 win 23040
+0    < P. 2049:3073(1024) ack 1 win 502
+0    > P. 2049:3073(1024) ack 3073 win 23040
+0    < P. 3073:4097(1024) ack 1 win 502
+0    > P. 3073:4097(1024) ack 4097 win 23040
+0    < P. 4097:5121(1024) ack 1 win 502
+0    > P. 4097:5121(1024) ack 5121 win 23040
+0    < P. 5121:6145(1024) ack 1 win 502
+0    > P. 5121:6145(1024) ack 6145 win 23040
+0    < P. 6145:7169(1024) ack 1 win 502
+0    > P. 6145:7169(1024) ack 7169 win 23040

+0    < . 7169:7169(0) ack 1 win 502
